Whether to use large pages or small pages is an area of tension between two opposing camps:

<a> TLB Coverage:
    % of the total VA covered by your TLBs. This demands that you have large pages

<b> Paging I/O && Internal Fragmentation
    These demand that the page size be small. Why? Because you writeback more data with large pages that have had small changes
    and the latter is obvious.


Contig bits in the TLB and TLB coalescing allows us to solve both. Which is what the GPUs do.

